      "notes": [
        "the p_p identity, taken together with the real-capital equation, implies negative output growth over this window. That is the documented over-determination, not a finding about the economy: the identity is reported and not enforced, so the calibration is unaffected.",
        "the identity corrections had to move materially away from one to fit the trajectory, the largest being p_b_scale at 5.308, a departure of 431%. A correction of one would mean the definitions of section 0.2 and the equations of motion agree; this is how far they do not. The correction is reported rather than constrained, because constraining it would make the calibration fail instead of making the inconsistency visible.",
